 A_{1G_k}=F_{k-1},\qquad A_{2G_k}=E\setminus F_k.$$

For $F=Y$ and for $F=Y^+$, every integral full or restricted star shift with $|l_j|\le S/N^{25}$ satisfies $$\label{eq:small-shift-ratio}
 e^{-N^{-8}}\le \frac{F(d(l))}{F(0)}\le e^{N^{-8}}.$$ For $(\kappa,A_\kappa)=(\omega,A_\omega)$ or $(\psi,J)$, on its corresponding star lattice, $$\label{eq:average-comparison}
 e^{-3N^{-8}}F(0)
 \le \frac{1}{A_\kappa}\sum_l\kappa(l)F(d(l))
 \le e^{3N^{-8}}F(0).$$ The lower bound remains valid if the sum is restricted to $\max_j|l_j|\le S/N^{25}$.

In block count coordinates, $g=\log\widetilde I_G$ is $C^3$, is concave, and satisfies, everywhere, $$\label{eq:smooth-derivative-bounds}
 |g''_{ij}|\le A_2=N^{800}/W^2,\qquad
 |g'''_{ijk}|\le A_3=N^{1250}/W^3.$$

For every nonempty input after the deterministic feasibility test, the preceding construction gives at most $2n$ paired ports of lengths $d_{iD}\le N^{21}W$, with $p=\sum d_{iD}$ polynomial in $N$, and a strictly positive weight $h$ on the entire slice <a href="#eq:paired-count-slice" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:paired-count-slice">[eq:paired-count-slice]</a>. For every real $s\in[0,1]$, $h^s$ has both integer signatures of Definition <a href="#def:integer-signatures" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="def:integer-signatures">7</a>. Its balanced mass $$\mathcal Z_{\rm port}
   =\sum_{\substack{(a,b)\in\mathcal S\\
                    a_{iD}+b_{iD}=d_{iD}\ \forall(i,D)}}h(a,b)$$ satisfies $|\log(\mathcal Z_{\rm port}/(JZ))|\le100N^{-7}$. These statements include $p=0$, when there is a single profile.

For every block and every port argument in its box, $$\label{eq:integral-bounds}
 e^{-N^{50000}}\le\widetilde I_G(u)\le e^K.$$ For the weight $h$ on the full paired slice of Proposition <a href="#prop:port-model" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:port-model">20</a>, $$\label{eq:weight-log-bound}
 |\log h(a,b)|\le N^{60000}.$$ All rational coefficients needed to define or evaluate its factors have polynomial encoding length in the input and in the query.

The polytope <a href="#eq:volume-lift" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:volume-lift">[eq:volume-lift]</a> has dimension $f+6m+d_0$, a polynomial facet-encoding bound, and an exact polynomial-time strong separation oracle. It contains a known rational ball of radius $1/32$ and has an outer ball of polynomial encoding length. Furthermore, $$\label{eq:volume-lift-accuracy}
 (1-\rho/10)\widetilde I_G(u)
       \le\mathop{\mathrm{vol}}(\mathcal Q)\le\widetilde I_G(u).$$ All polynomial bounds are in the original input length, the encoding lengths of $u$ and $\rho$, $N$, and $\rho^{-1}$, with absolute fixed exponents.
